The upstream source tree remains unmodified in the development checkout.
scripts/prepare-core.ps1 applies explicit adaptations to generated source:
transport injection; dependency-free diagnostics; safe disabling of external
program execution; strict unsupported-feature handling; RFC 1205 Query,
client reply, immediate/alternate read and Save Screen corrections; transparent
data handling; blink restoration; explicit code-page failure; Reset state.
src/core-adapter contains the replacement controller, logger and transport seam.

No upstream runtime JARs, Log4j, Jython, JT400, mail or PDF dependencies are
included in the application.

Packaged application images include complete application/build/test source and
the pinned upstream source under app/source, also supplied as Fish-source.zip.
Keep that matching source and these notices with redistributed application images.
Do not distribute just the executable or JAR without the corresponding source
and all applicable GPL obligations.

The bundled runtime is generated from Eclipse Temurin OpenJDK 25.0.5+8 LTS and
Gluon OpenJFX 25.0.3 by default (or the JDK/JavaFX explicitly selected for the
build). Their module-specific licenses and notices are in runtime/legal. OpenJDK
and OpenJFX use GPL version 2 with the Classpath Exception; see those notices.
Temurin and OpenJFX release/source information:
https://github.com/adoptium/temurin25-binaries/releases/tag/jdk-25.0.5%2B8
https://github.com/openjdk/jdk25u
https://github.com/openjdk/jfx
Use appropriately maintained JDK 25 / OpenJFX 25 builds for deployment and retain their notices.

src/native contains Fish's own Windows Kerberos, Shell shortcut, update
verification and compact native setup sources (compiled into fish-native.dll
and Fish-setup.exe). Window chrome uses OpenJFX 25 StageStyle.EXTENDED + HeaderBar
without custom Win32 WNDPROC subclassing or JAWT. The setup embeds a jpackage/WiX-generated
per-user MSI; Install-Fish.ps1 and fish.install.UserInstaller also support direct
non-admin per-user installation into %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\Fish.
Portable Zig and WiX are build tools retrieved from their official distributions
using checksums in tools.psd1; they are not application runtime dependencies.

Protocol references: RFC 1205, RFC 4777, RFC 854/855/856, RFC 885,
RFC 1091 and RFC 1572. These are referenced specifications, not bundled code.
